# Android release signing credentials — TEMPLATE.
#
# Copy this file to `keystore.properties` in this same directory
# (apps/vesper/src-tauri/gen/android/) and fill in the four values below.
# `keystore.properties` is gitignored: never commit it, and never commit the
# .jks/.keystore file it names. This template holds no secrets and is the only
# half that belongs in the repo.
#
# Without it, a RELEASE build fails with an explanation instead of quietly
# emitting app-universal-release-unsigned.apk. Debug builds do not read this
# file at all and keep using the SDK's debug key.
#
# Generate a release keystore once, and back it up somewhere you will still
# have in ten years — losing it means you can never update the published app:
#
#   keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore vesper-release.jks -alias vesper \
#     -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 10000
#
# NEVER point storeFile at ~/.android/debug.keystore, and never use the alias
# `androiddebugkey`. That key ships with the Android SDK, its password is
# published, and anyone can forge an update for an app signed with it. The
# build refuses both explicitly.

# Passwords do NOT have to live in this file. Each value can also come from
# (in precedence order, highest first):
#   1. a ${VAR} placeholder here, e.g.  storePassword=${MY_SECRET}
#   2. the well-known environment variables:
#        VESPER_KEYSTORE_FILE, VESPER_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD,
#        VESPER_KEY_ALIAS, VESPER_KEY_PASSWORD
#   3. a literal in this file (works, but move it when you can)
#   4. ~/.config/vesper-builder/signing.properties (same four keys, chmod 600)
# With the env vars or the local file supplying everything, this file can be
# absent entirely.

# Path to the keystore. Absolute, `~/…`, or relative to this directory
# (apps/vesper/src-tauri/gen/android/). Keeping the file OUTSIDE the checkout
# is the safer habit — and paths from the env or the local config MUST be
# absolute or ~/-relative.
storeFile=/home/you/keys/vesper-release.jks

# Password of the keystore file itself.
storePassword=${VESPER_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD}

# Alias of the key inside the keystore (`-alias` above).
keyAlias=vesper

# Password of that key. Often the same as storePassword; keytool asks for both.
keyPassword=${VESPER_KEY_PASSWORD}
